            methodology: 'NDVI is a band-ratio index that requires radiometrically calibrated and atmospherically corrected surface reflectance. Step-by-step: 1) Convert satellite DN to top-of-atmosphere reflectance; 2) Apply atmospheric correction (6S, FLAASH, or Sen2Cor); 3) Extract NIR and red surface reflectance; 4) Compute NDVI = (NIR−Red)/(NIR+Red). Time-series analysis requires compositing (e.g., 16-day MODIS NDVI) to remove cloud contamination.',
