            methodology: 'Mutual information is computed from the probability distributions. For discrete variables: I = Σ_i Σ_j p(x_i,y_j)·log₂(p(x_i,y_j)/(p(x_i)·p(y_j))). For continuous variables: the integral is approximated by binning or using kernel density estimation. For Gaussian systems (as in most data assimilation): I = ½·log₂(|P_f|/|P_a|) where P_f is forecast covariance and P_a is analysis covariance. The degrees of freedom for signal (DFS) = tr(I − P_a·P_f⁻¹) = 2·(I/ln(2)) for uncorrelated observations. For non-Gaussian systems: the mutual information is estimated using: (1) nearest-neighbor methods (Kraskov estimator), (2) copula-based estimation, or (3) variational inference.',
